{"name":"A Frond in Need","hex":"#9f9978","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The leaf of a fern, especially a compound leaf.","Any fern-like leaf or other object resembling a fern leaf."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frond"},{"term":"need","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A requirement for something; something needed.","A desire or craving for the satisfaction of a requirement perceived as essential or primal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have an absolute requirement for.","To want strongly; to feel that one must have something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/need"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frond","blocks":[{"text":"A frond is a large, divided leaf. In both common usage and botanical nomenclature, the leaves of ferns are referred to as fronds and some botanists restrict the term to this group. Other botanists allow the term frond to also apply to the large leaves of cycads, as well as palms (Arecaceae) and various other flowering plants, such as mimosa or sumac. \"Frond\" is commonly used to identify a large, compound leaf, but if the term is used botanically to refer to the leaves of ferns and algae it may be applied to smaller and undivided leaves. Whatever the term frond can also refer to structures or organisms of ediacaran lifeforms called Frondomorphs, which may be related to primitive animals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Davalia_frond_parts.png/330px-Davalia_frond_parts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frond","wikidata":"Q2333821"},{"title":"Need","blocks":[{"text":"A need is a requirement for survival or optimal functioning at a point of time and in a given context. Needs are distinguished from wants. In the case of a need, a deficiency causes a clear adverse outcome: a dysfunction or death. In other words, a need is something required for a safe, stable and healthy life while a want is a desire, wish or aspiration. When needs or wants are backed by purchasing power, they have the potential to become economic demands."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Need","wikidata":"Q190258"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Fern_frond_lobed.jpg/330px-Fern_frond_lobed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Fern_frond_lobed.jpg/330px-Fern_frond_lobed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A fern (Dryopteris decipiens) with simple (lobed or pinnatifid) blades, the dissection of each blade not quite reaching to the rachis.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFern_frond_lobed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg/500px-Fern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg/1280px-Fern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg/500px-Fern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A growing fern frond unfurling.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFern_Frond_Trichomes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Unfurling_Spiral_Fiddlehead_Fern_Frond.JPG/500px-Unfurling_Spiral_Fiddlehead_Fern_Frond.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Unfurling_Spiral_Fiddlehead_Fern_Frond.JPG/1280px-Unfurling_Spiral_Fiddlehead_Fern_Frond.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_